PLAINT FILED UNDER ORDER VII RULE 1 OF CPC

The Plaintiff respectfully submits as follows:

1. Jurisdiction of the Court

The suit schedule property is situated within the territorial jurisdiction of this Hon’ble Court. Hence, this Hon’ble Court has jurisdiction to try and entertain the present suit.

2. Description of Parties

The Plaintiff is the absolute owner and possessor of the suit schedule property. The Defendants are the original landowner and his brother, who are unlawfully interfering with the Plaintiff’s peaceful possession.

3. Facts of the Case

The Plaintiff purchased the suit schedule property bearing Survey No. ___, extent ___, situated at ___ Village, ___ Mandal, ___ District, through a registered Sale Deed dated ___, executed by a duly authorized General Power of Attorney holder of Defendant No.1, for valid consideration.

4. Validity of Title

At the time of purchase, the General Power of Attorney was valid and subsisting. The Plaintiff conducted due diligence and purchased the property in good faith. The Plaintiff has been in peaceful possession and enjoyment of the suit schedule property since the date of purchase.

5. Cause of Action

Subsequent to the purchase, disputes have arisen between Defendant No.1 and Defendant No.2 regarding internal family partition issues. Taking advantage of the said disputes, the Defendants have been unlawfully interfering with the Plaintiff’s peaceful possession without any right or title.

The cause of action arose on ___ when the Defendants first attempted to interfere and continues to arise on subsequent dates.

6. Illegal Interference

The Defendants have no manner of right, title, or interest over the suit schedule property after execution of the sale deed. Their acts of interference are illegal, arbitrary, and intended to harass the Plaintiff.

7. Necessity of Injunction

Unless the Defendants are restrained by an order of permanent injunction, the Plaintiff will suffer irreparable loss and hardship. The balance of convenience lies in favour of the Plaintiff.

8. No Other Suit

The Plaintiff submits that no other suit or proceedings are pending between the parties in respect of the suit schedule property.

9. Valuation and Court Fee

The suit is valued at Rs. ________ for the purpose of court fee and jurisdiction. Appropriate court fee is paid under Section 26(c) of the Telangana Court Fees and Suits Valuation Act, 1956.

10. Relief Sought

The Plaintiff therefore prays that this Hon’ble Court may be pleased to:

Grant a Decree of Permanent Injunction restraining the Defendants, their agents, men, or anyone claiming through them from interfering with the Plaintiff’s peaceful possession and enjoyment of the suit schedule property;

Award costs of the suit; and

Pass such other order(s) as this Hon’ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

